<!DOCTYPE qhelp SYSTEM "qhelp.dtd">
<qhelp>
  <overview>
    <p>
      Visual computer-use responses must preserve one response object from the
      provider through the native-image guard to the successful return.  A
      branch-only guard, wrong object, response replacement, success reset, or
      image removal can otherwise make text-only output look successful.
    </p>
    <p>
      The query follows local aliases and ordinary borrows with the Rust data
      flow library.  It trusts a guard only when its implementation still
      downgrades a response after missing-image output; unknown wrappers and
      collection semantics remain outside the claimed proof.
    </p>
  </overview>
  <recommendation>
    <p>
      Guard the exact response returned by every successful visual path, keep
      the guard on all paths to the return, and do not replace or mutate its
      success, error, or content-items fields after the guard.  Definite failed
      responses remain safe and are not reported as successful visual exits.
    </p>
  </recommendation>
</qhelp>
